        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manchester, New Hampshire; New England; northern New England; Northeast megalopolis\n- Topics: City size rankings; major cities and metropolitan areas\n\nFacts:\n- Manchester is the largest city in the U.S. state of New Hampshire.\n- Manchester is the eleventh largest city in New England.\n- As of 2016, Manchester was the largest city in northern New England, which comprises Maine, New Hampshire, and Vermont.\n- The Northeast megalopolis includes the major cities of Boston, Providence, Hartford, New York City, Philadelphia, Wilmington, Baltimore, and Washington, D.C.\n- The Northeast megalopolis also includes the metropolitan areas, suburbs, and many smaller urban centers associated with those major cities.",
